---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
import { appBySlug } from '../../data/apps';

const app = appBySlug('rejoiner')!;
const path = '/apps/rejoiner';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'apps/rejoiner');
const desc = description(site, 'apps/rejoiner');

const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can a Shopify team use Rejoiner without managed services?",
    "answer": "Yes. The platform and optional professional services are separate offerings. An internal operator can use the software; Strategy Partner adds guidance, while Creative Partner adds production and deployment scope."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the published price cover?",
    "answer": "The pricing page displays $25 per month at up to 1,000 contacts for the platform with unlimited email. Pricing depends on active contacts. Strategy Partner starts at $1,500 per month separately; Creative Partner is custom priced. Confirm the complete scope for your list."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does onboarding mean someone will write every email?",
    "answer": "No. Onboarding support and ongoing creative production are different commitments. Specify who writes, designs, approves and deploys each deliverable before comparing a services quote."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should cart recovery be evaluated?",
    "answer": "Rehearse an abandoned cart followed by purchase, an unavailable item and a restricted offer. Confirm the intended message, suppression and approval record. These are proposed checks, not reported merchant results."
  },
  {
    "question": "How does Rejoiner connect with Shopify?",
    "answer": "Rejoiner documentation lists a Shopify platform connector and Shopify journey webhooks for tags and discount codes. Validate the events and fields your own workflow needs rather than assuming every custom storefront event is included."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is SMS included in unlimited email pricing?",
    "answer": "The pricing page lists SMS separately per message plus carrier fees. An email subscription does not supply permission to text someone. Include message usage and the agreed operating responsibility in the budget."
  },
  {
    "question": "When is a services package useful?",
    "answer": "When the specific work it covers relieves a real team constraint at an acceptable cost. Compare available staff hours, production demand and approval capacity. There is no universal store revenue or order threshold."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can the merchant take operation back in house?",
    "answer": "Plan a handover of segment definitions, approved assets, journey diagrams, reporting definitions and access responsibilities. Confirm actual export formats and rights in the agreement; do not assume flows move automatically to another platform."
  },
  {
    "question": "What should determine renewal?",
    "answer": "Review agreed deliverables, reliability, staff time and contribution after costs alongside attributed revenue. A controlled comparison can inform incremental value; a dashboard total alone cannot establish it."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link" href="/apps">← All app reviews</a>
    <p class="editorial-kicker mt-6">Software and optional services</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{app.name} review for Shopify stores</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">Rejoiner offers ecommerce email software with optional Strategy Partner and Creative Partner services. The practical choice is how much execution your team wants to retain: operate the platform internally, buy guidance, or scope creative production and deployment with a service team.</p>
    <p class="mt-5 leading-8">Evidence checked November 25, 2026. This review uses supplier documentation and proposed evaluation scenarios; no merchant account tests or campaign outcomes are claimed.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose the operating model before the package</h2>
      <p>A home goods team might have a capable email operator but need help interpreting declining repeat purchases. That is a different purchase from a founder who needs copy, design and campaign deployment. Write a task inventory first: audience logic, merchandising brief, design, QA, approval, sending and measurement. Mark an owner and backup for each task.</p>
      <p>The positive value of optional services is flexibility in resourcing. Guidance can support an internal operator; creative execution can relieve a production bottleneck. Neither model removes the merchant’s knowledge of stock, shipping promises, product claims and margin constraints. A strong internal team can evaluate the platform on its own merits without assuming it must buy a retainer.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Published software and service scope</h2>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://www.rejoiner.com/pricing">Rejoiner pricing page</a>, checked November 25, 2026, separates contact-based software from professional services. Strategy covers reviews, reporting, deliverability monitoring and recommendations. Creative adds content, copy, design, development, QA and deployment. These are advertised inclusions, not evidence of results for a particular store.</p>
      <p>The <a class="link" href="https://docs.rejoiner.com/docs/getting-started">getting-started documentation</a> describes lists, segments, builders, broadcasts, journeys and reporting. These give an operator a foundation for both campaigns and lifecycle work. Check which parts of a proposed migration are onboarding work and which become recurring deliverables; a support conversation is not a signed production calendar.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Shopify data acceptance before creative approval</h2>
      <p>Rejoiner lists a Shopify connector. Its <a class="link" href="https://docs.rejoiner.com/docs/shopify">Shopify documentation</a> also describes journey webhook steps for customer tags and unique discount codes. A code must be available to the later message step; the documented inbound-webhook wait matters. Do not approve an offer by reviewing a static screenshot alone.</p>
      <p>Build a small acceptance sheet with a known cart, purchase, product variant, customer tag and subscription state. Compare event time and identifiers with Shopify. Include a guest who later signs in and an existing customer who declines marketing. The acceptance question is whether the intended person enters the intended journey with the right data, not whether a dashboard count looks plausible.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Home goods cart: offer authority and purchase suppression</h2>
      <p>Proposed exercise: a shopper leaves an $890 furniture cart, then buys before the next reminder. Check that the subsequent promotional recovery message is suppressed, that the cart link resolves and that shipping copy reflects the destination. Repeat with the item unavailable. Record the expected behavior and actual trace rather than declaring a recovery lift.</p>
      <p>For a 15% offer, the discount on $890 is $133.50. Ask finance which products can sustain that reduction and whether shipping, returns or sale exclusions change the rule. The merchant can approve an offer ceiling while the operator tests copy within it. This is a scenario-specific approval boundary, not a universal rule that every high-value cart needs a discount.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Cookware welcome: reviewing the creative service</h2>
      <p>Proposed exercise: brief a welcome message for premium cookware without an opening discount. Supply care instructions, approved product claims, image rights and a destination page. Compare the draft with the brief on a phone and with images blocked. Ask who corrects a missing care link and who can stop a scheduled send.</p>
      <p>A useful approval record names the version, audience, offer, expiry, reviewer and send owner. If a founder requests a late change to a product claim, the team should know whether that reopens QA. Agree revision scope and turnaround in the service agreement rather than assuming unlimited changes or a fixed response time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Fashion winback and beauty SMS coordination</h2>
      <p>For a seasonal fashion exercise, compare a styled full-price edit with a discount concept for lapsed customers. Define lapse relative to the catalog’s purchase cycle. Exclude recent buyers and check whether clearance stock changes the landing page before approval. This evaluates whether the brief can express margin and merchandising priorities without claiming a winning branch.</p>
      <p>For a beauty cart with separately consented email and SMS, map both messages on one timeline. Rehearse a purchase between them and an opt-out before the next send. Confirm who owns texts, replies and escalations in the chosen scope. Published SMS capability does not establish that every email services package includes a managed texting program.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Cost comparison with explicit assumptions</h2>
      <p>Use the actual platform quote for projected active contacts, then add optional services, SMS and fees, migration overlap and retained staff work. Compare this with the complete incumbent cost: software, agency scope and internal review time. Count retained work even if a supplier describes the service as hands-off. Avoid comparing an all-in service proposal with a bare software subscription.</p>
      <p>Illustrative budget only: assume a $200 platform allowance, $1,500 service allowance and 8 internal hours at $40. Total monthly operating cost is $2,020. These allowances are not a Rejoiner quote. If the alternative costs $1,200 with equivalent deliverables, the $820 difference requires additional contribution or labor value. At $41 contribution per genuinely incremental order, 20 extra orders cover $820 before other changes. At 10 extra orders, the shortfall is $410.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Measurement that distinguishes work from outcomes</h2>
      <p>Maintain two scorecards. The delivery scorecard tracks approved assets, corrected defects, launch readiness and unresolved decisions. The commercial scorecard tracks delivered messages, purchases, returns, discounts and costs. A supplier can complete useful work even when a small experiment cannot yet distinguish a sales effect.</p>
      <p>When feasible, compare eligible randomized groups with the same observation window, checking overlap with other campaigns. Record attribution rules before reviewing results. A change in seasonality or acquisition mix can explain a revenue change after migration. Do not turn a hypothetical target into a claim that Rejoiner generated it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Cutover and incident ownership</h2>
      <p>Inventory the old journeys, pending sends, suppressions and capture forms. For each replacement, name the person who pauses the incumbent and the person who enables the new flow. Check queued messages as well as active switches. A fixed multiweek overlap of identical cart flows can duplicate messages; use a controlled transition based on the actual queues.</p>
      <p>Rehearse a wrong offer, missing purchase event and unapproved draft. Identify a pause authority, a technical contact and the merchant decision maker. Agree seasonal availability and escalation against real needs. There is no evidence here for a universal launch date, response guarantee or required weekly meeting length.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Handover and renewal without a forced graduation path</h2>
      <p>Keep an accessible journey map, segment glossary, creative source files, suppression rules, experiment log and reporting definitions. Record which items can be exported and which must be rebuilt. Have a second operator explain a recent-purchaser exclusion and update an approved product link using the documented process.</p>
      <p>At renewal, choose continued services, a revised scope or internal operation from current economics and capacity. There is no automatic year-two migration or preferred destination. An ongoing service relationship can remain useful; a handover plan makes ownership clear when staffing or priorities change.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card mb-12">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-black">Related reviews and guides</h2>
      <ul class="mt-6 space-y-3">
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/sendlane">Sendlane review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">Sequenzy review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo review</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/compare/sequenzy-vs-klaviyo">Sequenzy vs Klaviyo</a></li>
        <li><a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Cart recovery guide</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Rejoiner Shopify FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
